# Radicale users: one "user:hash" line per person. Format is htpasswd.
# Copy to `users` (the real file is gitignored so hashes never get committed):
#   cp radicale/users.example radicale/users
# Generate a hash line:
#   printf '%s:%s\n' "you" "$(openssl passwd -6 'your-password')" >> radicale/users
# Result looks like:
#   you:$6$rounds=5000$abc...$xyz...
#
# An empty file means every login fails — a fresh deploy is closed by default.
